<html>
<title>How do I play the Studio II built-in games?</title>
<body>
<h1>How do I play the Studio II built-in games?</h1>

<p>
The sections below provide brief instructions on how to play the built-in games.
</p>

<p>
The descriptions below assume you are using a numeric keypad and have selected <strong>Settings/Use Numeric Keypad</strong>.
If this option is not selected, the alternative key is shown in parentheses.
For Player B, the keys <code>W</code>, <code>A</code>, <code>S</code>, <code>Z</code> control direction and <code>TAB</code> is used to fire. These keys work both with and without the <strong>Use Numeric Keypad</strong> setting enabled.
</p>

<h2>Doodle</h2>

<p>
Press <code>1</code> to start.
</p>

<p><strong>Controls</strong></p>

<pre>
Arrow Keys / Numpad 1-9   move dot
Numpad 5 (TAB)            start drawing
SPACE / Numpad 0          erase
</pre>

<p>
A white dot will appear in the lower left corner. Move the dot using the Arrow Keys or Numpad keys <code>1</code>-<code>9</code>.
Pressing two move keys simultaneously moves the dot diagonally across the screen.
</p>

<p>
By combining the functions of Doodle and Pattern, you can reverse the image, making your Doodle turn from a white drawing on 
a black background to a black drawing on a white background. Or, make just part of the screen white. You can even start 
another pattern and have the Studio II print over your Doodle.
</p>

<p>
After finishing your Doodle, press <code>2</code>. To reverse the image, first press the <code>Right Arrow</code> key. 
Then press <code>SPACE</code> or Numpad <code>0</code> and the screen will start to 'paint' itself white. 
You can freeze the picture any time by pressing Numpad <code>5</code> (<code>TAB</code>).
</p>

<h2>Patterns</h2>

<p>
Press <code>2</code> to start.
</p>

<p><strong>Controls</strong></p>

<pre>
Arrow Keys / Numpad 1-9   draw base pattern
SPACE / Numpad 0          generate pattern
Numpad 5 (TAB)            freeze pattern
</pre>

<p>
No dot will appear until a key is pressed. Form a simple design using the Arrow Keys 
(or Numpad <code>1</code>-<code>9</code>). To erase part of your design, simply trace back over it.
</p>

<p>
When your design is ready, press <code>SPACE</code> or Numpad <code>0</code>. The Studio II will repeat your design across the screen to form the pattern.
</p>

<p>
To 'freeze' the pattern, press Numpad <code>5</code> (<code>TAB</code>). Restart with <code>SPACE</code> or Numpad <code>0</code>.
</p>

<p>
After 130 key entries, the Studio II will start forming a pattern even if no <code>SPACE</code> is pressed.
</p>

<h2>Bowling</h2>

<p>
Press <code>3</code> to start. Players take turns rolling the ball.
</p>

<p><strong>Controls</strong></p>

<pre>
Player A
--------
Up Arrow      hook up
SPACE         straight
Down Arrow    hook down

Player B
--------
Numpad 8 (W)      hook up
Numpad 5 (TAB)    straight
Numpad 2 (Z)      hook down
</pre>

<p>
The game consists of 10 frames.
</p>

<h2>Freeway</h2>

<p>
Press <code>4</code> to start.
</p>

<p><strong>Controls</strong></p>

<pre>
SPACE         start car
Up Arrow      increase speed
Down Arrow    brake
Left Arrow    steer left
Right Arrow   steer right
TAB           difficult start
</pre>

<p>
The score is given after 2 minutes.
</p>

<h2>Addition</h2>

<p>
Press <code>5</code> to start.
</p>

<p><strong>Controls</strong></p>

<pre>
Player 1      keyboard keys 0-9
Player 2      Numpad 0-9 (P Q W E R T Y U I O)
</pre>

<p>
Add the digits shown in the middle and press the appropriate key.
The quicker you answer, the more points you receive. The game lasts for 20 numbers.
</p>

</body>
</html>
